From e5b99e62fecb9c2daf842fe7e64060d02fb5ab3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 21:06:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH net v1 0/2] bpf, sockmap: fix TCP partial read handling

Sockmap verdict processing can run on TCP skbs after userspace has
already consumed part of the skb through the native receive path. The
current code assumes the whole skb is unread, which can either advance
copied_seq over bytes that were already read or deliver those bytes a
second time through SK_PASS.

Patch 1 makes tcp_eat_skb() account only the unread receive sequence of
the skb.
Patch 2 trims local SK_PASS self-ingress data by copied_seq in both the
direct ingress path and the queued backlog path.

This intentionally limits the fix to the TCP partial-read cases. It does
not include the broader SK_PASS followed by SK_DROP/SK_REDIRECT receive
ordering changes or teardown pending-sequence accounting.

Dong Chenchen (2):
  bpf, sockmap: account only unread data in tcp_eat_skb
  bpf, sockmap: trim self-ingress SK_PASS by copied_seq

 include/net/tcp.h  | 23 ++++++++++++++++
 net/core/skmsg.c   | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 net/ipv4/tcp_bpf.c | 10 ++++---
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

